Fix CI: doctest 2.4.12, scope warnings to our targets, format the tree

The first CI run failed on every platform for two independent reasons, plus
the formatting job was misconfigured. All three are fixed and verified.

1. CMake 4.x dropped compatibility with projects that declare
   `cmake_minimum_required(VERSION < 3.5)`. doctest 2.4.11 declares 3.0, so
   configuration aborted on every platform. Bumped the pin to doctest 2.4.12,
   which declares 3.5.

2. Warning flags were set with `add_compile_options()` in FESettings.cmake.
   That form is directory-scoped but inherited by every subdirectory below it,
   so `-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic` leaked into the FetchContent dependencies and
   GLFW's Wayland backend failed under `-Werror=unused-parameter`. This
   violated the documented policy that third-party code never gets our flags.
   Warnings are now applied per-target via the `fe_warnings` interface target
   only; the dependency include directories (glfw, nlohmann_json, glad, stb)
   are marked SYSTEM. `fe_mark_system` now resolves ALIAS targets, since it is
   passed `nlohmann_json::nlohmann_json`.

   This also surfaced genuine first-party warnings that were previously hidden
   because the leak failed the build first: an unused parameter in the Node
   attach/detach hooks, a shadowed constructor parameter, and ignored
   [[nodiscard]] results in two tests.

3. The clang-format job used a job-level `continue-on-error`, which is not a
   valid key for that context, and the apt clang-format version varies by
   runner image and disagrees with the checked-in .clang-format. The job now
   installs a pinned `clang-format==23.1.3` and the tree is formatted with it,
   so the check is a real, deterministic gate.

Verified: clean configure and build with -DFE_WARNINGS_AS_ERRORS=ON on
CMake 4.4.4 / GCC 14; no third-party or first-party warnings; 60 unit test
cases (2218 assertions) pass; graphics tests pass with a display and skip
cleanly without one.
